Z||000003||Oreif||04-26-2000||09:56 AM||||Go ahead and race him! I think the biggest engine available for 87 Trans Am is the 305 V-8. These were not the most powerful V-8's. Also if he has some milage on it the 305's were notorious for worn camshafts. I would race him like 1/8 mile. Once you hit 80mph his cubic inches will take over. But odds are you will be 2-3 carlenghts ahead. The 350 F-bodies came out in 89 these were definately faster.||||reg||4
Z||000004||Standard||04-26-2000||02:34 PM||||Yeah, that's what I thought... He lives in wisconsin and my family went there for easter, I had to work so I couldn't go.  My brother said he want's to race me.  I asked if he had a 305 or 350, but my bro didn't know.  I'll race for fun if I can find some time to get out there.||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||04-26-2000||05:32 PM||||Is his car TPI or carbed?  More than likely it's TPI.  I had an 85 IROC with the auto\305 TPI and it was really weak 0-60.  Those cars only ranked 215-225hp, and most had 2.73 non-posi's.  If he's got 2.73's and an auto, I think you'll have him.  3.42's might be close...  He's got the torque advantage as well, but he also weighs about 3400lbs.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RobertVol||04-26-2000||09:40 PM||||Just a Small correction ..the 88 's had 350's.....Had a 88 GTA with tpi ..pretty "quick" car. not fast.just quick. But faster than a GT. the 87 305 tpi came with max 225 hp. but torque was around 300 - 325 lb ft. It actually was a mean little car in the formula firebirds. lighter and with the stick. Just a clarification  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||04-27-2000||01:11 AM||||they did't have that much torque man.... My old LT1 had 275hp and 325ft lbs of torque.  The 350 was an OPTION from '87 up.||||reg||1
Z||000008||GT Bastard||04-27-2000||01:12 AM||||Most GTA's were 350's yeah..  There were a small number of 5sp 305 cars though.||||reg||1
