Z||000010||RobertVol||04-28-2000||12:12 AM||||YEs the torque on a firebird formula was well into 300 lb ft. the horspower was lower but the torque was there. I had one ....her you go ....#########'s<P>Type Displacement Horsepower Torque Induction  <BR>OHV V-8 305/5.0 155@4200 245@2000 4 bbl  <BR>OHV V-8 305/5.0 165@4400 250@400 4 bbl  <BR>OHV V-8 305/5.0 205@4400 285@3200 TPI  <BR>OHV V-8 350/5.7 210@4000 315@3200 TPI  <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||GT Bastard||04-28-2000||01:15 AM||||I realize the 350's had great torque, but I'm talking 305's.  Most Formula Firebirds were still 305's.  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||RobertVol||04-28-2000||09:23 AM||||285 lb ft is nothing to sneeze at. But if its not a formula and its a T/a which kets see.....yeah it is...with the extra weight yeah he could be close but still would not be able to stay to long if its the 305 TPI. with the stick thats still a legite 60 time of 7.2. but you right would closer than first thought. ||||reg||1
